    "Stem": "Riverview Industries operates three business segments: consumer products, industrial equipment, and a medical device division. The medical device division was classified as held-for-sale six months ago after the board determined its disposal represents a strategic shift. The buyer's financing has encountered repeated delays, and the transaction is now expected to close in nine months. Meanwhile, the consumer products segment sold a small product line that generated 3% of total revenue. The controller must recommend the appropriate financial statement presentation. Which recommendation complies with ASC 205-20?",
