    "Stem": "CONTROLLER MEMORANDUM — Ridgeview Manufacturing\n\nTO: Controller Sarah Okonkwo\nFROM: Financial Reporting\nRE: Consolidation Assessment — Axion Tech Equity Investment\n\nRidgeview holds 45% of Axion Tech's outstanding common stock ($3,200,000 investment, equity-method accounted). However, Ridgeview's CFO sits on Axion's 5-member board and, through a separate contractual agreement, holds veto power over Axion's operating budget, major capital expenditures, and CEO compensation. Axion is a variable interest entity (VIE): its equity at risk ($2,800,000) is insufficient to finance its activities without additional subordinated financial support; Ridgeview provided a $4,500,000 loan guarantee that absorbs Axion's expected losses; and Axion's activities are conducted primarily on Ridgeview's behalf under a manufacturing services agreement. No other investor holds protective rights comparable to Ridgeview's. The external auditors have requested Ridgeview's consolidation analysis. Ridgeview's general counsel argues that 45% ownership is below the traditional 50%+ voting interest threshold, so consolidation is not required. Ms. Okonkwo asks: 'Under ASC 810, is Ridgeview required to consolidate Axion, and under which consolidation model?'",
