      "B": "Consolidate Axion under the VIE model. As the primary beneficiary of a VIE, Ridgeview has both (a) the power to direct the activities that most significantly impact Axion's economic performance (through board veto rights, budget authority, and the manufacturing services agreement) and (b) the obligation to absorb losses or the right to receive benefits that could be significant to Axion (through the $4,500,000 loan guarantee). The 45% equity ownership is secondary to the VIE analysis.",
      "C": "Consolidate Axion under the voting interest model. Although Ridgeview owns 45%, the board seat plus CFO veto rights collectively constitute de facto control equivalent to majority ownership. The VIE analysis is unnecessary because the voting interest model captures control through direct and indirect voting rights, including contractual governance provisions.",
