    "ExplanationCorrect": "Under ASC 810-10-45, noncontrolling interest (NCI) represents the portion of equity in a subsidiary not attributable to the parent. In consolidated financial statements, the parent reports 100% of the subsidiary's assets, liabilities, revenues, and expenses regardless of ownership percentage. The NCI is then presented as a separate component of equity in the consolidated balance sheet, distinct from the parent's shareholders' equity. It is not reported as a liability because the parent has no obligation to transfer assets to the noncontrolling shareholders. It is also not reported as revenue because NCI represents an ownership claim, not an income stream of the parent. This presentation provides users with a clear picture of the total equity of the consolidated entity, showing both the parent's and the noncontrolling shareholders' interests.",
