      "B": "Recommend IFRS reporting because IAS 38 allows capitalization of qualifying development costs, which better reflects the economic value created by Axion's investments. Under IFRS, the $3.2 million would be recognized as an intangible asset and amortized over the software's useful life, providing a more faithful representation of the company's financial position and the future benefits expected from its development pipeline.",
