    "ItemType": "MCQ",
    "ItemStyle": "single-select",
    "Stem": "Delta recorded gross sales of $354,000, sales returns of $14,600, and sales allowances of $6,300. What net sales should be reported?",
    "Choices": {
      "A": "$333,100",
      "B": "$354,000",
      "C": "$339,400",
      "D": "$362,300"
    },
    "CorrectChoice": "A",
    "ExplanationCorrect": "Net sales represents gross sales revenue reduced by all contra-revenue accounts, primarily sales returns and sales allowances. Sales returns occur when customers return previously purchased goods for a refund, while sales allowances represent price reductions granted to customers for defective or damaged goods that the customer agrees to keep. Both returns and allowances reduce the total revenue the entity ultimately earns from sales transactions. For Delta, gross sales of $354,000 are reduced by sales returns of $14,600 and sales allowances of $6,300. The calculation is: Net Sales = $354,000 - $14,600 - $6,300 = $333,100. This net sales figure is the amount reported as the top line of the income statement and provides a clearer picture of the revenue actually retained by the entity from its core sales activities.",
