    "CorrectChoice": "D",
    "ExplanationCorrect": "Basic EPS = (Net income - Preferred dividends) / Weighted-average common shares outstanding. Preferred dividends of $30,000 are subtracted because they are not available to common shareholders. Income available to common = $330,000 - $30,000 = $300,000. Weighted-average shares reflect time-proportionate ownership: 100,000 shares outstanding for the full year, plus 22,000 additional shares issued July 1 and outstanding for 6 months, contributing 11,000 weighted-average shares (22,000 x 6/12). Total weighted-average shares = 100,000 + 11,000 = 111,000. Basic EPS = $300,000 / 111,000 = $2.70 per share. EPS is a widely cited performance metric but should be interpreted alongside cash flow and capital structure metrics. Exam trap: using ending shares (122,000) or beginning shares (100,000) instead of the time-weighted average, or omitting the preferred dividend deduction.",
