    "ExplanationWrongC": "Switching costs and relationship value are legitimate factors, but estimated at $125,000-$200,000 for first-year transition versus ongoing annual savings of approximately $190,000 from AdvantEdge's quality and delivery advantages. Over a 3-year contract, even with $175,000 of transition costs, the net benefit of switching to AdvantEdge is approximately $395,000 ($190,000 x 3 - $175,000). More importantly, staying with Nova means accepting a 1.2% defect rate (vs. 0.6% for AdvantEdge) and 2.5% late-delivery rate (vs. 0.8%) for three more years — on the single most critical direct material. Supplier evaluation under management accounting principles considers total cost of ownership over the contract life, not just transition costs in the first year. Relationship value is real but must be weighed against quantifiable performance differences that directly affect production continuity and rework expense.",
