    "Stem": "Bayshore Manufacturing's four-person accounting department handles all vendor payments. Staff A enters vendor invoices into the system, approves them for payment, and executes the electronic funds transfers. Staff B reconciles all bank statements monthly and investigates discrepancies. Staff C prepares journal entries and posts them to the general ledger. Staff D manages the fixed asset subledger and calculates monthly depreciation. During the most recent internal audit, the auditor noted that Staff A processed a $34,000 payment to a vendor that had no purchase order, no receiving report, and was not in the approved vendor master file — the payment was discovered only when the vendor sent a refund check three weeks later, stating the payment was made in error. Analyze the segregation of duties deficiencies: which staff member holds the most incompatible combination of duties, and what is the minimum personnel reassignment needed to achieve adequate segregation given the four-person constraint?",
